#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171898 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "91f986c6-c305-50eb-a5b7-36043279d128" :question/math-academy-id "e-9505" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_1 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u + v \\\\ v - 2 u + 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_2 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u - v \\\\ v - u\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_3 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ u - {v}^{2}\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171899 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9779a982-2048-58e2-8a90-df2bcb366d96" :question/math-academy-id "e-9506" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} = \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}5 & \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{a} \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b} & 4\\end{array} \\right]} \\cdot {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]}+\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 6 \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c}\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} \n= {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 u + v - 6 \\\\ 2 u + 4 v\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171900 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2ddc4e15-3729-5425-953c-1cb95edc201b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9508" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} = \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & - 5\\end{array} \\right]} \\cdot {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]}+\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297ef899-ffab-5f8e-937b-d760e3330734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761739} {:answer/id #uuid "9e00db59-4dc2-5af0-953d-729ddec5e15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e00db59-4dc2-5af0-953d-729ddec5e15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761740} :answer-field/id #uuid "f081b937-a6d7-5a80-bcec-3683c58195c0" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bf8a28f-d14a-5b6a-a8a0-fc0cd375f5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761742} {:answer/id #uuid "d2884c78-349d-5b0c-9eba-d3889bb3f522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bf8a28f-d14a-5b6a-a8a0-fc0cd375f5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761742} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f99474f-009d-5351-8af6-1a14b4bac668" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2} \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a0b8788-1fe9-5e3d-9b6c-6f8c1f469e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761745} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbcc2bf-e877-5fe0-b527-d99ddf8494f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbcc2bf-e877-5fe0-b527-d99ddf8494f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761746} :answer-field/id #uuid "f461a493-52ce-57b0-bc9e-2bea49146fd7" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d581310-6942-54b8-b545-b203d0da1352" :question/math-academy-id "q-124007" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ -u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term ${u}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6609faf5-218c-5c18-93e2-43f7844cd543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257682} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb52f73-b59b-5559-a1a9-0a3e40afda0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257877} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bcc0cb-9c0c-5351-b203-fb02bf523336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258387} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f6db9c-5b9d-5bd9-a019-2b86dc159910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258611} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ab26a8-fcba-5abc-9df8-f8a6a45e0da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6609faf5-218c-5c18-93e2-43f7844cd543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257682} :answer-field/id #uuid "471f200c-b9c9-5e1b-b46b-262099bea64a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b49d315-187b-5a70-8690-97b6311cd839" :question/math-academy-id "q-124088" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=u-2v+1,\\,y=u+v-2\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v \\\\ u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003c72ab-a274-52ab-aa2c-2593da45d334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256784} {:answer/id #uuid "7e750f7c-8312-5236-a7f3-e877f7f70512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257905} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ab775c-a099-5165-bdb5-243b28bd32ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258236} {:answer/id #uuid "dee951d0-1321-54ed-8801-95e0057779e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258724} {:answer/id #uuid "eb76beb7-5c43-55e3-8818-e328ff068342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e750f7c-8312-5236-a7f3-e877f7f70512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257905} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c09496-ed8d-5b09-8ce6-b28b1163e1a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01d5649d-0bb8-52a3-be74-234b60c39fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124091" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-u+av+b,\\,y=2u-5v+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+4v \\\\ 2u-5v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+4v+2 \\\\ 2u-5v+1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-u+4v+2,\\,y=2u-5v+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+2+1=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f49e56-4b49-5907-af3c-90093546b298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761820} {:answer/id #uuid "702ea799-8924-5435-975e-aaeb5bb90bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "702ea799-8924-5435-975e-aaeb5bb90bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761821} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5ba73c-904e-59fa-89bb-505277772dba" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "413efea3-9096-5e67-9a28-7ab1d9f2080b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761823} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c23afc-814d-5482-8ccc-3ed5e385e94c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "413efea3-9096-5e67-9a28-7ab1d9f2080b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761823} :answer-field/id #uuid "f431f2e4-96bc-5398-a8f6-2e24117b25ae" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv+1 \\\\ u-2v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cab3c43-f16a-5045-8f62-2dafb2e785ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761826} {:answer/id #uuid "02fbb4aa-5bdc-5aa3-8d46-6936230ab888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02fbb4aa-5bdc-5aa3-8d46-6936230ab888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4a59b7a-6da1-5b76-bf9c-c557310f0ef8" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5cb4053-f0cc-5e78-b06a-329e6bd661d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124255" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u+v \\\\ -u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{3}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "051434b8-c984-5c6a-8955-1f0b60930d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256829} {:answer/id #uuid "2752c7eb-4676-56ab-b0cd-1bf9a38e162f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257126} {:answer/id #uuid "59eb0a37-274e-5830-8b80-ff23964f5119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257562} {:answer/id #uuid "81280065-bedd-5f73-8e81-255309fdda87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257929} {:answer/id #uuid "e993acbd-20a6-5dc9-8643-05cf5a9fa4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e993acbd-20a6-5dc9-8643-05cf5a9fa4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258811} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0be749e-1222-5271-990b-b7537ef677e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9882bc48-ffe2-5a96-827b-d1eb44c92577" :question/math-academy-id "q-124271" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+4v,\\,y=-5u+bv+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-3u+4v,\\,y=-5u+3v+0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-3+3+0=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2565bba5-5eac-5cdf-86de-6ce6f7d0d3b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257099} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba6f2e5-650b-5a1e-987d-fbf362041044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257314} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccad9ff-665f-52f7-90d6-bb242d608429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257741} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebaf9c7-1edf-584c-8b9b-b5af17d2eab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257758} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4687f8-a5a9-54bc-b0a0-64f52c2b2036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba6f2e5-650b-5a1e-987d-fbf362041044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257314} :answer-field/id #uuid "498afc40-c208-5e2f-a071-6c4f2ca45dea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8d697d1-ccf8-518a-9776-12fda551dcda" :question/math-academy-id "q-124291" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u+3,\\,y=7v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u \\\\ -u+7v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=5+(-1)+3=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ecd5138-97c9-5f1d-9f65-cc0d9b8ce532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761757} {:answer/id #uuid "08ed3589-2339-5743-bc8c-050c02986f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ecd5138-97c9-5f1d-9f65-cc0d9b8ce532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761757} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d50fe7-0274-5bc6-a0e1-40b50e7324f4" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ \\sqrt{v}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35046b3a-a056-5db9-b417-2ddd3127c1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761760} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa6b9bb-fb83-5008-a38a-347efb58c363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35046b3a-a056-5db9-b417-2ddd3127c1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761760} :answer-field/id #uuid "d16d1973-8e63-5276-aad6-7274d76258be" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+1 \\\\ {v}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a785eb4f-94c2-504f-8710-4da7ed3f10a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761763} {:answer/id #uuid "219a85e2-c268-5442-9168-583f067360d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "219a85e2-c268-5442-9168-583f067360d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761764} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a047ff5-9231-5f15-9d46-36d8e99a0bad" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd962593-19ff-5124-a324-851d683c9d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-124236" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\sqrt{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c48763d7-6d11-5b61-99d8-33d0e6f77f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761766} {:answer/id #uuid "da089761-ad8a-5162-ae94-da63244f038d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da089761-ad8a-5162-ae94-da63244f038d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761767} :answer-field/id #uuid "0106f1ec-8ddf-57f3-b1c5-4984106635b6" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91f1e704-b0f3-5a36-bdda-0d6b48b57695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761769} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e2e053-40ad-5a2b-86c6-7b5d9222a41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6e2e053-40ad-5a2b-86c6-7b5d9222a41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761770} :answer-field/id #uuid "11324aa4-7009-5571-a615-cac582314fa3" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc18460b-d79a-5201-81c7-6c75c68a7a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761772} {:answer/id #uuid "4d653ce7-9791-552c-afc7-c0aa1ab1a042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc18460b-d79a-5201-81c7-6c75c68a7a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761772} :answer-field/id #uuid "767f80e8-5b9a-5388-9e28-83a7813f107e" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61d7ee8c-7043-59bf-884d-8cfd140d0d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-124237" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3de5f97a-e701-5701-a05c-23c22bef8357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761784} {:answer/id #uuid "138fef99-01db-513e-a29d-01e425b60fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "138fef99-01db-513e-a29d-01e425b60fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761785} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9df2c9-552a-511e-9205-37615f8c0034" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3898dc2-f21e-57ca-9143-6ac4b4882bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761787} {:answer/id #uuid "0b352b37-07df-5320-8ea7-963035d954da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b352b37-07df-5320-8ea7-963035d954da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761788} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bfaa05c-e473-5f98-95f5-d6859a038d68" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f02990c5-34dc-50b5-af81-290bd2b4f70e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761790} {:answer/id #uuid "98c6b326-e5f6-534c-9db1-ef5f7bdbe39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c6b326-e5f6-534c-9db1-ef5f7bdbe39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761791} :answer-field/id #uuid "32705d53-51c5-5ae1-8ac4-49cf0e0b9867" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a803158d-6736-5561-9888-f16b39fbcde9" :question/math-academy-id "q-124245" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9u+8v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4dd585b-d7d6-565c-8526-6f807421e5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761793} {:answer/id #uuid "b80a8623-b019-5241-93ab-98afe607ed43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b80a8623-b019-5241-93ab-98afe607ed43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761794} :answer-field/id #uuid "97921a3d-e7ba-5bfb-8ee6-61f686f102e7" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e90c4b-43b7-5a13-8336-ad66179679ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761796} {:answer/id #uuid "9b888229-3827-58de-861c-fcf1683e0098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e90c4b-43b7-5a13-8336-ad66179679ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761796} :answer-field/id #uuid "39d73c41-4145-5ce2-a14b-0540f66c3b74" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761798} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d41830e4-9137-5476-b4a1-82b463cd4050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761799} {:answer/id #uuid "9795dc6c-3bff-5dcb-9298-087e30fdf0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d41830e4-9137-5476-b4a1-82b463cd4050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761799} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f6159a2-1858-5d4d-b0eb-c0b276e2d1d6" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f56913d5-4faa-5365-a00a-436d31c63ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124247" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae6d0fda-615a-5d78-981c-77a0cd470c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761802} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec49183-0b58-5724-83f6-612a15e768f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae6d0fda-615a-5d78-981c-77a0cd470c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761802} :answer-field/id #uuid "f72cf4b9-78c1-5f2c-a6f3-29cea6e051a5" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ca6dee-8517-58cb-8b3d-585f3ddc6c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761805} {:answer/id #uuid "a5cccff2-fa71-5c44-aa3e-2cb64439faee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5cccff2-fa71-5c44-aa3e-2cb64439faee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761806} :answer-field/id #uuid "acef1447-62d5-5dfe-b78f-46b560261dab" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761807} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f54c0a1c-9764-5d72-bf58-b610a17ed884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761808} {:answer/id #uuid "67a1db19-1d19-550d-bd40-860f5274e5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67a1db19-1d19-550d-bd40-860f5274e5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761809} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66e8f3b-7535-5214-8814-34b3ad6cc716" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d7af34-5a26-56da-8335-dcbefb3a99a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124251" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic terms ${u}^{2}$ and ${v}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4u+6v \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5e54913-380a-5c6e-883b-ed8dc28cda6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761811} {:answer/id #uuid "d1068765-e19f-5dc2-a914-1ec7523b54bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5e54913-380a-5c6e-883b-ed8dc28cda6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761811} :answer-field/id #uuid "0801b5a5-4022-56ac-8ddd-313b94868746" :answer-field/key "${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761813} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3dda847-3c1e-58bd-acdd-193bd1451a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761814} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0d0260-c675-5c00-9ed7-8864057b2325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0d0260-c675-5c00-9ed7-8864057b2325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761815} :answer-field/id #uuid "d82c66c1-288e-5a76-9ca0-df862ce8bb58" :answer-field/key "${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200efa28-008f-54c1-9375-35299b6dc116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761817} {:answer/id #uuid "6d331c79-dc8f-50aa-a257-80c4c5776925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "200efa28-008f-54c1-9375-35299b6dc116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761817} :answer-field/id #uuid "dceadc50-364c-5347-a00b-abc019ff9f03" :answer-field/key "${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186761819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d494b59f-56bb-56d7-a682-8c7f88848b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124253" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227340af-71d1-5d08-ace5-1c9258c8fcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257065} {:answer/id #uuid "30bb3807-55a5-5cda-b326-fdec9c047352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257211} {:answer/id #uuid "41438c81-cf63-57d7-afc0-35b56a8a92f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257363} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37718-f272-5547-a58a-87b172f20251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258850} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd38fa9-a703-5a9b-9e62-e43d804d84e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37718-f272-5547-a58a-87b172f20251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258850} :answer-field/id #uuid "e68f436c-5c06-5c77-ab1f-cbf71cb2e171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "248bc276-68c1-5b41-9594-c7af8b2e1b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-124259" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e740d3a-5c03-5dd2-816a-487643106091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257194} {:answer/id #uuid "33a79aaa-17fe-5ec0-9815-f48d8949b65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257239} {:answer/id #uuid "73970941-5456-5fe8-906f-5e233465ae16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257796} {:answer/id #uuid "9158f20d-6a83-542a-9c54-77af73ba69ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258067} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7c1236-c621-5444-b1e2-cd41e1db1cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce7c1236-c621-5444-b1e2-cd41e1db1cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258575} :answer-field/id #uuid "671307a9-23d3-54b5-988a-ecf7a2f8a2ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ded880b4-9f04-5275-85c1-4486642a0a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-124261" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv-2,\\,y=u+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6u+8v \\\\ u\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6u+8v-2 \\\\ u+5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=6u+8v-2,\\,y=u+5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+8+5=19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fe1c6ee-1822-5943-a4ab-95e2e8729c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257204} {:answer/id #uuid "42afdead-f7ba-55b9-837b-58a7ebcab735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257371} {:answer/id #uuid "5b54affb-22be-504f-9fc3-75ecc52418c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257578} {:answer/id #uuid "d4002265-2697-5e13-a97a-e4de62345ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258638} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d00b3d-b50a-5be5-8ad2-4acce9512f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3d00b3d-b50a-5be5-8ad2-4acce9512f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258912} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d42c87d-8e24-585c-849a-f00efbd599ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18f13e13-3246-593c-9da3-b608f58de1b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124262" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+v,\\,y=bu+cv\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-2u+v,\\,y=9u+3v\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+9+3=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e5d8b9-aa23-509f-9d82-cbc0a58b88aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257118} {:answer/id #uuid "523c5ff0-288c-54a6-8984-dab86593561a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257483} {:answer/id #u