trix}-6u-2v+1 \\\\ 4u+7v-2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-6u-2v+1,\\,y=4u+7v-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+1+7=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "343b2207-66d5-57bb-87f6-c4c790c690d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257244} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7ec3bd-0bf2-5983-a44c-e00a3fdf0ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258277} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e42a09-6baf-5d36-87f3-f42986684931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258323} {:answer/id #uuid "f23f4bbb-43d3-539b-a8e2-405d7732b7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258890} {:answer/id #uuid "f6097032-0646-54a4-8dab-1221f0240b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab7ec3bd-0bf2-5983-a44c-e00a3fdf0ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258277} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca41ba6d-3943-5258-9ae3-5aaa5c4554e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31239ffb-2521-5f24-adb5-1bf7dc8cd57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124284" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca5b200-1e86-5077-aeb8-b67c50a6c8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256904} {:answer/id #uuid "10c3ff93-d73d-554e-87b3-0212fbed198e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256936} {:answer/id #uuid "27911809-e171-5b95-b3fb-a9b7e21c7cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 